---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · RoomBeat Zero Telemetry Audit"
  description="RoomBeat privacy commitment: 100% on-device operation, zero tracking pings, zero accounts, zero analytics."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <div class="op-eyebrow">
      <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#118d4f]"></span>
      <span>LEGAL &amp; PRIVACY AUDIT</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="op-title mt-3 text-3xl font-normal text-[#062314] sm:text-5xl">
      Zero Telemetry Policy
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-[#626b60]">
      EFFECTIVE DATE: OCTOBER 2026 · AUDIT STATUS: 100% OFFLINE VERIFIED
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-8 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-[#35433a] border-t border-[#e0e2d3] pt-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-[#062314]">1. Core Architecture: Zero Data Leaves Your Local Network</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[#35433a]">
          RoomBeat is an entirely decentralized peer-to-peer audio rig designed for local network (LAN) and portable Wi-Fi hotspot operation.
          It does not connect to any central cloud server, does not relay audio packets over the internet, and sends zero analytics or telemetry pings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-[#062314]">2. No Accounts or Identity Collection</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[#35433a]">
          You are never prompted to create an account, log in, or provide an email address, phone number, or name.
          Room connection codes (QR and 6-digit numeric PINs) are generated client-side using cryptographic pseudo-random number generators (`SecureRandom`) and are never stored on any remote server.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-[#062314]">3. Android Permissions Explained</h2>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-2 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="rounded-[2px] border border-[#e0e2d3] bg-[#fbfbf7] p-3">
            <span class="font-bold text-[#062314]">FOREGROUND_SERVICE_MEDIA_PROJECTION:</span>
            <span class="text-[#626b60] block mt-0.5">Required on Android 14+ to keep the audio capture pipeline active while music plays in background.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-[2px] border border-[#e0e2d3] bg-[#fbfbf7] p-3">
            <span class="font-bold text-[#062314]">ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK (Android 17+ / API 37):</span>
            <span class="text-[#626b60] block mt-0.5">Required to bind local UDP sockets for multicast playback and discover nearby phones via mDNS.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-[2px] border border-[#e0e2d3] bg-[#fbfbf7] p-3">
            <span class="font-bold text-[#062314]">POST_NOTIFICATIONS:</span>
            <span class="text-[#626b60] block mt-0.5">Displays the system media notification and persistent room control controls in the notification drawer.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-[#062314]">4. Open Source Verification</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[#35433a]">
          Every line of RoomBeat’s Android client and NDK C++ codebase is published on
          <a href="https://github.com/WantedChip/RoomBeat" target="_blank" class="text-[#118d4f] font-semibold underline">GitHub</a>.
          You can inspect the source code, verify that no network telemetry endpoints exist, and compile the APK directly from source using Android Studio.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
